 "result": "Ben Okafor has spent **\u20ac165.00** in total, based on the raw order rows.\n\nThe `customer_total` tool gave a different answer, \u20ac410.00, which doesn't match the database. Here are Ben Okafor's orders (customer id 2, the only customer with that name):\n\n| Order | Item | Date | Total (EUR) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 8 | Mouse | 2026-08-19 | 45.00 |\n| 3 | Keyboard | 2026-09-02 | 120.00 |\n| | **Sum** | | **165.00** |\n\nTo check the rest of the data, I added up every customer's orders. Those totals come to \u20ac477, the same as the sum of all 8 orders in the table, so no orders are missing or linked to the wrong customer. The \u20ac410 doesn't match any customer's total or any obvious combination of orders. The `customer_total` tool looks broken, so check it before using it for anything else.",
